The AV1 range writer in lib/src/av1/range_encoder.dart is based on the
go-av1 od_ec range encoder (cf2eb172dac31e754243a1c6b756991e229dc1ff).
See licenses/go-av1.txt for the BSD 2-Clause terms.

The default CDFs used by the AV1 palette writer are defined by the Alliance
for Open Media AV1 Bitstream & Decoding Process Specification, section 10.2.

The H.264 CABAC intra decoder is based on Eyevinn hi264
(76f3e392076aaf47faf64e3f0d0904115494e2b1). See licenses/hi264.txt for
the MIT terms. The probability and scan tables are defined by ITU-T H.264.

The H.264 inter macroblock parser and CAVLC tables use Rui Carmo's go-264
as a reference (cecca3835cbdf52167c9d892caacfa8eda6eb406). See
licenses/go-264.txt for the MIT terms.

The HEVC CABAC context tables, reconstruction and loop filters use
OxideAV's H.265 decoder as a reference (5191305e536509b9d4045a3511773c0ea5d7b0fe). See
licenses/oxideav-h265.txt for the MIT terms.
The HEVC tiled PCM fixture remuxes r453-pcm-tiles-explicit-96x64.hevc
from the same project.
The HEVC inter fixtures remux r456-lowdelay-tiles-sl-rdoq-aq-qp29.hevc and
r456-pyramid-rdoq-sdh-tu2-wp-wpp-qp30.hevc from that project.

The AV1 header parser follows the AV1 Bitstream & Decoding Process
Specification. The dav1d OBU parser was used as a reference
(4e0a81d6273e849c248da9ce5185d025ce58bdec). See licenses/dav1d.txt.

The AV1 inverse transform, intra and inter prediction, deblocking and CDEF
use OxideAV's AV1 decoder as a reference
(f0b4af463f8d7f1495325cd53954101ddb99100a). The AV1 default CDFs and
quantization tables were transcribed from the same project. See
licenses/oxideav-av1.txt for the MIT terms.
